[REQUIREMENT]
UID: REQ-ROO-174
STATUS: Active
TITLE: REQ-ROO-174: Request pity and lobby priority are scored by calendar day and reset after a win
STATEMENT: >>>
Request pity and lobby priority are scored by calendar day and reset after a win
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
domain: Auction/Requests
priority: unspecified
type: system
constraints: Calendar day is row.date if it parses, else row.eventDate. Accepted forms: YYYY-MM-DD and M/D/YYYY. Unparseable dates are ignored.; Lookback is priorityLookbackDays clamped to 1–365; unset uses 30. Inclusive window is today-(days-1) through today in the guild timezone. Days after today are excluded.; Order inside the window is calendar day, then write-time decoded from the row id, then the id string.; Selected and Reset end the streak. Absent ends it unless the item is high value. High-value Absent counts as one night and does not end the streak.; After the last ending row, each distinct calendar day of NotSelected counts 1. Pending, Superseded, and Canceled neither count nor end. The same night counts once.; Commit and reset-priority store eventDate as the ISO session date: parsed targetSessionDate, otherwise the guild calendar day.
acceptance_criteria: A Selected (or Reset, or non-high-value Absent) on a later calendar day than a NotSelected yields pity 0 for that member and item, even when the win row's id sorts before the loss id. | Two NotSelected rows on the same calendar day contribute 1, not 2. A Pending or Canceled row on another day contributes 0. | For a high-value item, an Absent night plus a later NotSelected night scores 2, and the Absent does not end the streak. For a non-high-value item the same rows score 1 (only the NotSelected after the Absent). | The request lobby, Mimic standings, Discord request snapshot, and auction auto-commit leaderboard show this live score on pending bids, not the priority number stored on the pending row. | A pending bid and a Selected row for the same member, item, and calendar day show priority 0. | Committed web_requests (Selected, NotSelected, Absent, Superseded) and an officer priority-reset row carry eventDate set to that ISO session date. | Request History renders eventDate when it is non-empty and '---' when it is empty.
source_draft: delta-2026-10-03/mints.json
ssot_status: published
sot: Develop@9b8e7ae9ca2f9ccf046c5b609cdda545ced6eae9
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: USR-ROO-023

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: REQ-ROO-179
STATUS: Active
TITLE: REQ-ROO-179: Review Allocation and the Live Auction announce are per-item rows
STATEMENT: >>>
Review Allocation and the Live Auction announce are per-item rows
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
domain: Auction/Requests
priority: unspecified
type: software
constraints: Only items with lootSummary qty > 0 are listed.; Selected rows are the unique non-empty uids in categoryAllocations[itemId].selected, ordered by rank then uid.; Not-selected rows are rankingsByItem[itemId] minus those uids, in ranking order.; Rank label is the 1-based index in that item's ranking, padded to 2 digits, or an em dash when the uid is not in the ranking.; Priority is the lobby detail priority, or 0 when missing. One row per item and member, not per loot slot.; Discord mentions snowflake uids; other uids are shown as display name. Messages chunk at 2000 characters.
acceptance_criteria: Review Allocation selected and not-selected tables have columns #, Item, Member, Priority, and do not have a Requested column. | The same member selected on two loot items appears twice, once per item, instead of once in a unique-member list. | An item with no loot qty does not appear. | The GEN-room Live Auction message lists those same rows as '#{rank}  **{item}**  {member}  Prio {n}' under the existing selected and not-selected sentences, not as mention columns of unique members.
source_draft: delta-2026-10-03/mints.json
ssot_status: published
sot: Develop@9b8e7ae9ca2f9ccf046c5b609cdda545ced6eae9
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: USR-ROO-022

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: REQ-ROO-180
STATUS: Active
TITLE: REQ-ROO-180: Confirm Allocate saves the session, then announces from the server
STATEMENT: >>>
Confirm Allocate saves the session, then announces from the server
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
domain: Auction/Requests
priority: unspecified
type: system
constraints: POST /api/requests/announce-allocate accepts no client winner list. Body may be empty.; Officer check uses configuration adminRoles via the Discord officer check. No session identity is 401. Non-officer is 403.; No active_session is 400 with error 'No active Mimic Book session.'; Discord 'not configured' is 400; offline, not connected, rate-limited, or temporarily blocking is 503; not found is 404.; Confirm writes activeStep 2, the preview loot summary, category allocations, initial winners, active matrix filter, and sidebarTab 'standby' before announcing.
acceptance_criteria: Confirm Allocate does not call the announce route when the session write fails, and the officer sees 'Session saved locally, but the server write failed. Discord announce skipped.' | When the session write succeeds, Confirm Allocate posts /api/requests/announce-allocate and the GEN-room message is built from the stored session plus the current request lobby (REQ-ROO-179 rows). | Announce Live Auction posts that same route without requiring the confirm-modal save. | While the announce is in flight the confirm button reads 'Allocating…' and is disabled.
source_draft: delta-2026-10-03/mints.json
ssot_status: published
sot: Develop@9b8e7ae9ca2f9ccf046c5b609cdda545ced6eae9
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: USR-ROO-022

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: REQ-ROO-181
STATUS: Active
TITLE: REQ-ROO-181: Mimic Book does not re-GET the session while the page stays open
STATEMENT: >>>
Mimic Book does not re-GET the session while the page stays open
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
domain: Auction/Requests
priority: unspecified
type: software
constraints: GET /api/requests/active-session ETag is 'empty' when no session exists, otherwise s:{version}:{lastUpdated}.; A matching If-None-Match returns 304 with an empty body and Cache-Control private, no-cache. The 24-hour auto-reset in REQ-ROO-083 still applies on a real GET.
acceptance_criteria: Leaving Mimic Book open does not issue a repeating GET of /api/requests/active-session. | The session is loaded when the signed-in user identity for the page changes. | A client that repeats the GET with the current ETag receives 304 and no session body.
